      "widgets_values": [
        "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is Yan Qing, the same young East Asian man as the first-frame reference: same face, short black hair, small old scar above the outer end of his left eyebrow, plain dark casual clothing. He remains on frame left on the customer side of the counter, facing the butcher. He makes only a small natural mouth movement for the order, then watches the parcel attentively. No broad smile, no camera-facing pose, no movement to the other side of the counter.\n<Subject 2> is the same stocky middle-aged East Asian butcher shown on frame right in the first-frame reference, wearing the same navy work shirt and worn dark-brown apron with faint old stains. He remains behind the counter and does the wrapping action with both hands. His expression is sincerely pleased with a restrained natural smile, never a sales grin.\n<Subject 3> is the single large pork parcel already on the counter in Picture 1, being wrapped in plain kraft butcher paper. Keep its size and position consistent; do not create more parcels or expose a second piece of meat.\n<Subject 4> is the same pork stall from Picture 1: same pale tiled counter, wooden door, red pendant-lamp glow, hanging meat and sausage string, same first-light timing and screen directions.\n<Picture 1> fixes the final framing, camera position, faces, wardrobe, lighting and starting hand/parcel positions. Do not reframe, widen, zoom or cross the counter axis.\n\nsummary:\nA single fixed medium-wide shot of the purchase transaction. Yan Qing orders fifty jin of pork. The butcher acknowledges him and calmly completes wrapping the one parcel already on the counter. Yan Qing stays in place and watches. The parcel remains on the counter at the end; no handoff or bicycle appears in this shot.\n\nretention_analysis:\nBoth men keep the same identity, face, hair, wardrobe, body proportions and screen side throughout. The butcher stays frame right behind the counter; Yan Qing stays frame left in front of it. The stall anchors and practical warm light do not change. Only the butcher's hands fold the existing paper around the existing single parcel; Yan Qing makes one small speaking gesture and then stays still. No camera movement, cut, zoom, axis crossing, extra person, duplicate hand, extra parcel or new prop.\n\ndetailed_description:\nPhotorealistic live-action drama, candid and understated, matching the first-frame reference and previous shot's realistic market world. Static eye-level medium-wide camera from the same side of the 180-degree axis. Keep both men's faces readable in profile/three-quarter view and the counter visible across the lower frame. The five red pendant lamps, centered dark wooden door, white tiled counter, hanging cuts and sausage string remain stable. Warm practical stall light is dominant with only faint cool dawn spill. This is an ordinary story scene, not a commercial: no hero product pose, no product close-up, no presenting the parcel to camera.\n\nOne uninterrupted 7.29-second action:\n0.0-1.5s Yan Qing looks toward the butcher and says clearly in Mandarin: “老板，给我来五十斤猪肉。” He stays in place.\n1.5-2.1s The butcher gives one small acknowledging nod and replies: “好嘞。”\n2.1-6.2s Without changing position, the butcher smoothly folds the loose kraft paper around the one parcel already in front of him, using both hands. The movement is continuous and economical, not a rapid montage. Yan Qing watches without reaching over the counter. The pork tray and all stall anchors remain where they are.\n6.2-7.29s The butcher completes one final paper fold and rests both hands beside the wrapped parcel. He says naturally in Mandarin: “小伙子，以后多光顾啊！” Yan Qing remains attentive. End with the wrapped parcel still on the counter, ready for the next shot's handoff.\n\nNo subtitles, captions, readable signs, logos, app UI or watermarks. Voice quality is not being evaluated in this visual test; retain the exact Chinese dialogue instead of describing silent speech.",
